We say that $G$ has \emph{property RD} if there exist $C>0$ and $s\ge0$ so that, for all $f\in \mathbb{C}[G]$, we have
\begin{equation}\label{eq:rd}
\|f\|_r\ \le\ C\,\|f\|_{H^s}.
\end{equation}
Replacing $(C,s)$ by $(\lceil C\rceil,\lceil s\rceil)$ preserves \eqref{eq:rd}, so we assume throughout that $C\in\mathbb{N}$ and $s\in\mathbb{N}$.  We call the pair $(C,s)$ a pair of \emph{RD constants} for $G$.
